  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment history shows negative sentiment (e.g., -0.25 or 0.00 with recent declines) to avoid overestimating price stability.",
    "Reduce forecast volatility in early periods (e.g., first 5-7 days) when sentiment is neutral or positive, as models tend to overreact to short-term noise.",
    "When sentiment shifts to positive (e.g., 0.50), increase forecast mean slightly to reflect bullish momentum, but cap upward movement to avoid overshoot.",
    "Apply mean reversion correction if forecast deviates >10% from recent 5-day average, especially after sharp spikes or drops.",
    "For long-term forecasts (e.g., 30-day), reduce forecast magnitude if sentiment is neutral or negative, as market tends to consolidate or decline.",
    "Avoid over-optimistic forecasts after recent price spikes — reduce forecast peak values by 5-10% to account for market correction."
  ]
}
